# Email / Nodemailer SMTP Configuration
# In development:
# - Leave SMTP_HOST blank to use the safe development fallback (jsonTransport in-memory mock).
# - To inspect real emails in development, configure an SMTP testing service:
#   * Mailpit (local): SMTP_HOST=localhost, SMTP_PORT=1025 (no user/pass required)
#   * Mailtrap / Online SMTP testing: SMTP_HOST=sandbox.smtp.mailtrap.io, SMTP_PORT=2525, SMTP_USER=..., SMTP_PASS=...
# In production:
# - A real SMTP transport is required; fallback is disabled.
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_SECURE=false
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
SMTP_FROM_EMAIL=no-reply@parkease.com
SMTP_FROM_NAME=ParkEase

# Local Mailpit Executable Path (optional, for auto-starting Mailpit with development server)
# Leave blank if Mailpit is in your system PATH, or specify full executable path:
# Windows example: MAILPIT_PATH=C:\Mailpit\mailpit.exe
# macOS/Linux example: MAILPIT_PATH=/usr/local/bin/mailpit
MAILPIT_PATH=C:\Mailpit\mailpit.exe
